---
import BaseLayout from "src/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Landing from "@components/Landing.astro";
// Optimize our landing image and pass it as props to the BaseLayout (for preloading) and Landing (for rendering)
import {getOptimizedImage} from "@libs/utils"
import landingImage from "@assets/images/landing/desert.jpg";
const optimizedImage = await getOptimizedImage(landingImage)
import client from "@data/client.json";

---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy | R &amp; R Marketing" description="How R &amp; R Marketing handles website inquiries, form details, and measurement data." preloadedImage={optimizedImage}>
  <Landing title="Privacy Policy" image={optimizedImage} compact />
  <article class="privacy-copy container mx-auto px-4 py-8 max-w-3xl">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p>This notice describes information handled through remediationrestorationmarketing.com, the website of {client.name} (R &amp; R Marketing).</p>

    <h2>Information you provide</h2>
    <p>Our inquiry forms collect the details you enter, such as your name, email address, phone number, company, service territory, and the services you are interested in. Other forms may collect a message, budget range, or email address for a resource or newsletter signup.</p>
    <p>On the two-step strategy-call form, if you complete your contact details and continue to step two, those details may be saved when you leave the page even if you do not submit the final request. This lets us follow up about your interest. Please avoid including sensitive personal information in website forms.</p>

    <h2>How information is used and handled</h2>
    <p>We use inquiry information to respond, discuss your territory and marketing needs, and follow up on your request. Resource forms collect your email address to handle your signup. Netlify hosts the website and processes form submissions, including submissions forwarded by our server functions.</p>

    <h2>Website and advertising measurement</h2>
    <p>The website uses Google Analytics and Google Ads tags to measure visits, page and form interactions, phone-link clicks, and accepted requests. Google tags can use cookies and collect browser, device, and interaction information. An accepted form request is measured separately from a booked call or a qualified lead.</p>
    <p>We also use Matomo Cloud for website measurement. The site loads a Matomo tracker for page visits and link interactions. When JavaScript is disabled, a tracking image can send a page visit to Matomo.</p>
    <p>We store advertising click identifiers, campaign parameters, and the landing-page path in your browser's session storage and include them with inquiry submissions to understand where inquiries came from. Session storage also holds submission identifiers and confirmation flags to limit repeated conversion events. The paid-page form's custom measurement events use interaction labels and submission identifiers rather than the contact details you type.</p>
    <p>Read <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a> and <a href="https://www.netlify.com/privacy/">Netlify's privacy notice</a> for more about those providers.</p>

    <h2>Booking and other external services</h2>
    <p>The confirmation page embeds Google Calendar for booking. Some pages can load a YouTube video when you choose to play it. These providers handle information under their own policies. Information you provide when booking is handled through Google Calendar separately from the website inquiry form.</p>

    <h2>Your choices and questions</h2>
    <p>You can manage cookies and website storage through your browser settings. Blocking them can affect website measurement or functionality. You can contact us with questions about information you have provided, or to request access, correction, deletion, or an end to follow-up. Contacting us does not require submitting another website form.</p>
    <p>Email: <a href={`mailto:${client.email}`}>{client.email}</a><br />Phone: <a href={`tel:${client.phoneForTel}`}>{client.phoneFormatted}</a></p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .privacy-copy { overflow-wrap: anywhere; color: #1f2937; line-height: 1.7; }
  .privacy-copy h1 { font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 5vw, 2.5rem); margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .privacy-copy h2 { font-size: 1.4rem; margin: 2rem 0 .75rem; }
  .privacy-copy p { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .privacy-copy a { color: #075ca8; text-decoration: underline; }
</style>
